description:
MailboxName carries a is_internationalized: bool internal field (line 236) that gates whether the mailbox can match an rfc822Name SAN (ASCII only) or only an SmtpUTF8Mailbox SAN (RFC 8398).

Callers — e.g., a CA that wants to *issue* a cert and know in advance which SAN form to use, or a logging layer that wants to record 'this validation was for an internationalized address' — cannot read this flag back without re-running parse() and inspecting through the verify path.

Combined with PKIX-68mt.18 (no accessors generally), this is the most visibly missing accessor on the type because it's a documented public behavior of verify_mailbox: 'An internationalized MailboxName (non-ASCII local-part) can only match an otherName(SmtpUTF8Mailbox) SAN entry' (rustdoc lines 455-458). The user is told what the type does based on this flag but cannot observe the flag.

Trivial fix:

  impl MailboxName<'_> {
      pub fn is_internationalized(&self) -> bool { self.is_internationalized }
  }

Severity P3 (folded into PKIX-68mt.18's accessor surface, but worth calling out separately because the docs already promise behavior gated on this hidden flag — that's a contract leak).
